# AMD64 thunk export spec -- kernelbase.dll.
#
# kernelbase matters because a modern CRT imports the loader surface from HERE,
# not from kernel32: find.exe called kernelbase.GetModuleHandleW and then
# kernelbase.GetProcAddress.  Those two are namespace-sharp and are answered by
# the dispatcher's thunk_overrides (see dlls/ntdll/signal_ppc64.c), which must
# carry a kernelbase row for every sharp export -- a plain pass-through hands
# the guest a native ppc64 code address to CALL.
#
# Until this file existed kernelbase was the ONE module a staged file in
# C:\windows\sysx8664 could serve, because no builtin outranked it.  Now the
# builtin does, and there is exactly one way any thunk module reaches a guest:
# built here, served from the build/install tree like every other builtin.
DLL kernelbase.dll
FROM-SPEC auto
